@title Electronic health record downtime
@subtitle Runbook for charge nurses and front-desk staff, Pelican Bay Clinic
@author Clinical Operations
@date 2026-11-15

kpi Declare after | 10 min | record unavailable or slow
kpi IT service desk | ext. 5000
kpi Paper scans due | 4 hours | after restoration

!!! The allergy list in the downtime binder is the source of truth until the record is back.

## Declare downtime

Downtime is declared when the record has been unavailable or unusably slow for 10 minutes.

1. The charge nurse announces "Paper procedures" on the overhead page.
2. The charge nurse calls the IT service desk on extension 5000.

## During downtime

1. Switch to paper
-- Take the downtime binder from each station. It holds the printed schedule refreshed at 05:00 daily, an allergy list and a medication list for every patient booked that day.
-- Label every paper form with a patient label sheet.
2. Check in patients
-- Confirm identity with two identifiers: name and date of birth.
-- Record the arrival time by hand.
3. Orders and medications
-- Write down every verbal order and read it back.
-- Never give a high-risk medication without a second nurse's check.
-- Record every dose on the paper medication sheet.
4. Keep care moving
-- Do not cancel visits solely because of downtime.
-- Tell patients about any delay beyond 20 minutes.

## Recovery

1. When IT announces restoration, wait for the all-clear before entering anything.
2. Scan paper documents into the record within 4 hours.
3. Reconcile medication entries within 24 hours.
4. Report the event on the incident form.

